================================================================
4. KEY CONVERSIONS APPLIED
================================================================

SQL Syntax Conversions:
  - SCOPE_IDENTITY() → RETURNING clause (writable CTEs)
  - GETDATE() → NOW()
  - IDENTITY(1,1) → SERIAL
  - NVARCHAR → VARCHAR
  - BIT → BOOLEAN
  - DATETIME → TIMESTAMP
  - BEGIN TRANSACTION/COMMIT → Writable CTEs (for ADO.NET compatibility)
  - DECLARE @var → Writable CTEs with subqueries
  - CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE → CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION ... LANGUAGE plpgsql
  - SYSTEM_USER → CURRENT_USER
  - IF NOT EXISTS (sys.objects) → DROP ... IF EXISTS
  - GO statements → Removed
  - SQL Server triggers → PostgreSQL trigger function + CREATE TRIGGER

Schema Object Names:
  - All table, column, and object names converted to lowercase
  - Products → products, ProductId → productid, etc.

